/* book exam traps: Calling the easting and northing rows 'attributes'. They are the spatial half; the properties below them are the attribute half. | Joining ward '07' to numeric 7 without converting one side. Join keys must have the same type and a clean value. | Treating ward 7 as a ratio value and averaging ward numbers. Ward is a nominal label, not a quantity. | Mixing an attribute query with a spatial query. "Depth > 60 m" tests a field; "inside ward 7" tests coordinates against a boundary. Once the answer is stored as a ward field, "ward = 7" is an attribute query that copies an earlier spatial result. | Assuming a feature has one fixed primitive. A town or road can be a point, a line or a polygon at different scales. */
